{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795224,"nonce":"XPwVNIiE1BpNPfnrqA7YwihPEk8=","title":"Support custom OBS destinations and validate additional streaming adapters","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P3\n\nScope\nOffer a generic destination/profile path for a user's preferred OBS-supported streaming service without requiring Twitch/YouTube identity. Expose stream start/stop/status and configured viewing links while clearly declaring unavailable chat/account capabilities. Document the extension contract for additional adapters such as Kick or self-hosted services; validate each official API before promising parity. Automatic multi-destination restreaming is separate scope.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nA fixture custom destination works through an existing OBS profile with keys hidden and no incorrect provider controls. Users can change providers independently of their room identity and other collaborators. Unavailable viewing links and driver failures have useful states. An adapter conformance fixture demonstrates extension-owned registration/cleanup without changing the Jam protocol.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}